	(text "Indicators -- status LEDs (D2, D3)"
		(at 30.48 25.40 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
		)
		(uuid "11111111-0000-4000-8000-000000000001")
	)
	(text "Placement only: no wires or global labels yet, same convention as this\nboard's other unwired sheets.\n\nD2 = charge status, driven from MCP73831 STAT (U2 pin 1,\npower_bms.kicad_sch), which is currently unconnected. STAT is a tri-state\noutput; Microchip's own typical application circuit (DS20001984H) drives an\nLED from VDD through a series resistor to STAT. R10 = 1k gives roughly 3mA\nat the ~5V VBUS rail -- confirm the exact rail and value at wiring time.\n\nD3 = system status, intended to be driven from a NINA-B111 GPIO so firmware\ncan indicate powered / ranging / fault. GPIO not yet allocated.\n\n0603 LEDs here rather than the bay station's 0805, since the wristband is\nthe size-constrained board. Series resistors are 0603 per the project\nstandard. Both LEDs are low-current by design -- the wristband runs off a\nsmall cell and indicator current is not free."
		(at 30.48 33.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "11111111-0000-4000-8000-000000000002")
	)
